  "source": "Not captured: no house here owns a Zaptec (D4 §5.9, D-0081's precedent, D-0371). Written from custom-components/zaptec v0.8.7 (github.com/custom-components/zaptec, tag v0.8.7): the entity set and classes from sensor.py, number.py, switch.py, binary_sensor.py, button.py and update.py (CHARGER_ENTITIES on the charger, INSTALLATION_ENTITIES on the installation); the names from translations/en.json with _attr_has_entity_name = True (entity.py); the charger's via_device is its installation (manager.py, create_entities_from_zaptec); the Charger mode options are the API's ChargerOperationModes lower-cased (ZaptecSensorTranslate, README 'Changes from 0.7.x to 0.8.x'); Available current's max is the installation's MaxCurrent (number.py). The states are a car charging at 16 A on a 3-phase IT 230 V installation.",
